 "López-Zubero’s brother, " [:a {:href "\\athletes\\show\\46551"} "David"] ", had won Spain’s first ever swimming medal back in 1980 with a bronze in the 100 butterfly, but they were basically American with dual citizenship. They had both been born in the United States, raised in the US, trained in the US, and went to American colleges. However, their father was Spanish which gave them a Spanish passport and allowed them to compete internationally for Spain. David had chosen this route first and Martín followed it."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "153"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/46550"} "Martín López-Zubero"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ESP"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ESP.png"}] "ESP"]] [:td {} "1:59.22 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:58.47 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "192"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/50062"} "Vladimir Selkov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/EUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/EUN.png"}] "EUN"]] [:td {} "1:59.81 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:58.87 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "355"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/48472"} "Stefano Battistelli"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "1:59.56 (3 h6)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:59.40 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"